// A filter: copy standard input to standard output, one line at a time.
//
// readln() returns one line without its trailing newline, or the empty string at
// end of input. eof() reports whether stdin is at end of input WITHOUT consuming a
// character, which is what lets the loop terminate.
//
// Run it with input piped in, since eof() blocks on an interactive terminal until
// a character is available:
//
//     echo < input.txt

while not eof() do
    call println(readln())
end
